{
 "ep": 18,
 "title": "What If You Healed 1,000,000x Faster?",
 "script": "What if your body healed a million times faster? Not ten times. A million. Day one, you get a paper cut, and it closes before the blood even reaches your fingertip. Day two, you crash your bike, and your scraped knees are gone before you stand up. Your best friend Leo stares. Dude, do that again. Day three, a car window shatters over a crying little girl. You cover her, and your cuts close before she stops crying. But then something weird starts happening. You're starving, all the time. Six breakfasts before lunch, and you're still hungry. Because your body builds new skin and bone out of food. That's why doctors feed people with bad burns way more than normal. Day six, you jam your finger in a car door, and it heals in three seconds, before anyone can straighten it. A bone that heals in the wrong position stays that way. Crooked for good. Day nine, hiking with Leo, the trail crumbles. Your leg snaps, bent the wrong way, and it's already healing. Hold it straight, and it heals perfectly. But Leo is sliding off the edge, clinging to a root above a rocky drop. Help! I'm slipping! Let go of your leg to grab him, and it heals bent. You'd limp for the rest of your life. Ten seconds. Nine. Eight. The root is cracking. Seven. Six. Your bone is setting. Five. Four. Leo's fall, or your leg forever. Do you let go of your leg?",
